The port adapts the upstream PCCS API, input validation, PCS requests, cache
policies, collateral import, and certificate selection. Relevant upstream
sources include service/routes, service/controllers, service/constants,
service/services (including caching_modes), service/pcs_client, and
service/pckCertSelection. Their adapted portions are in internal/server,
internal/service, internal/pcs, and internal/collateral.

internal/collateral/selection.go and tcb.go translate the PCK selection and
TCB comparison logic from service/pckCertSelection/pckCertSelection.js and
Tcb.js. Selection tests adapt upstream cases. These upstream files are
Copyright (C) 2025 Intel Corporation.

internal/collateral/testdata/pck_certificates.json copies the eleven PCK
certificate fixtures from service/pckCertSelection/pckCertSelection.test.js,
Copyright (C) 2025 Intel Corporation. See the adjacent README.txt for their
test-only purpose. They are not trust anchors supplied for deployment.

Intel notices are retained for upstream-derived material. They do not
attribute the independent Go implementation or its maintenance to Intel.
This distribution does not bundle Intel enclave binaries or the Node.js
service and its npm dependencies.
